From d1ad2d1ce0d92f4848e1e20c752811cc479894c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:40:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] audiopolicy: declare the USB module in the generic policy
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AudioPolicyManager opens exactly the modules the top-level
audio_policy_configuration.xml includes, and AOSP's generic file lists only
primary and r_submix. Installing audio.usb.default without this line therefore
changes nothing observable: the HAL is present, never opened, and every capture
keeps being served by the primary STUB, whose in_read() does memset(buffer, 0,
bytes) after a usleep() that fakes a real device's pacing. An app recording the
microphone gets a perfectly timed stream of zeros and no error anywhere.

Patching the generic file rather than installing a replacement is deliberate and
was arrived at the expensive way (bd remora-4ei.37). remora.mk registers the
frameworks/av/services/audiopolicy/config soong namespace, and soong emits an
install rule for every prebuilt_etc in a registered namespace REGARDLESS of
PRODUCT_PACKAGES — proven on a2dp_audio_policy_configuration.xml, which has a
rule while being in no PRODUCT_PACKAGES and required by nothing. So a
PRODUCT_COPY_FILES onto /vendor/etc/audio_policy_configuration.xml is always a
second rule for one target and kati refuses at parse time. This file is the
module's own src (via the :audio_policy_configuration_generic filegroup), so
editing it keeps exactly one rule and changes what it installs.

Change-Id: Ied5b64dfaba81ef35135c6a27b78cacee72212df
---
 .../config/audio_policy_configuration_generic.xml          | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/audiopolicy/config/audio_policy_configuration_generic.xml b/services/audiopolicy/config/audio_policy_configuration_generic.xml
index 9ad609df2b..297510b289 100644
--- a/services/audiopolicy/config/audio_policy_configuration_generic.xml
+++ b/services/audiopolicy/config/audio_policy_configuration_generic.xml
@@ -27,6 +27,13 @@
         <!-- Remote Submix Audio HAL -->
         <xi:include href="r_submix_audio_policy_configuration.xml"/>
 
+        <!-- USB Audio HAL. Remora (bd remora-4ei.37): AudioPolicyManager opens exactly the
+             modules this file includes, so without this line audio.usb.default is installed
+             and never opened, and every capture keeps coming from the primary STUB — whose
+             in_read() memsets the buffer to zero on a faked clock, i.e. an app records
+             perfectly timed silence and nothing reports an error. -->
+        <xi:include href="usb_audio_policy_configuration.xml"/>
+
     </modules>
     <!-- End of Modules section -->
 
-- 
